From 57be4ff5ec551d6ab711a60163ce32591c950015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:54:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/59] pci: the BARs of a device of class 0xFF

pciscan read and sized the base address registers only for the classes
it lists; a device that fits no class (0xFF: Realtek's PCI Express card
readers, RTS522A and others) kept p->mem[] empty, its driver found no
registers.  Class 0xFF is read as the others now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/9/port/pci.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sys/src/9/port/pci.c b/sys/src/9/port/pci.c
index d35e71bd5..12a65bd25 100644
--- a/sys/src/9/port/pci.c
+++ b/sys/src/9/port/pci.c
@@ -603,6 +603,7 @@ pciscan(int bno, Pcidev** list, Pcidev *parent)
 			case 0x0F:		/* sattelite communication controllers */
 			case 0x10:		/* encryption/decryption controllers */
 			case 0x11:		/* signal processing controllers */
+			case 0xFF:		/* fits no class (Realtek's card readers) */
 				if((hdt & 0x7F) != 0)
 					break;
 				rno = PciBAR0;
-- 
